---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import ContactInvitation from './ContactInvitation.astro';
import architecture from '../assets/matterfield/matter-architecture.png';
import {getIndustries} from '../data/content';
interface Props {draft?:boolean;}
const {draft=false}=Astro.props;
const fields=await getIndustries(draft);
---
<Layout noindex={draft} title='Company' description='NRTH Inc. is an independent company bringing distinct venture directions together across six fields. Meet the thinking behind NRTH.'>
 {draft&&<aside class='preview-banner'><a href='/preview'>Editorial workspace</a><span data-preview-status>Draft preview</span></aside>}
 <section class='page-heading'><span class='section-label'>The company</span><h1>Not one lane.<br/><em>A wider world.</em></h1><p>NRTH is an independent company with room for different disciplines, unfamiliar questions and new ways of seeing the work.</p></section>
 <figure class='wide-art' data-image-reveal><Image src={architecture} alt='Conceptual graphite architecture with a narrow orange-lit passage' widths={[640,1100,1600]} sizes='90vw' format='webp' loading='eager'/><figcaption>Conceptual architecture — a visual study of space and possibility.</figcaption></figure>
 <dl class='facts-list'><div><dt>Company</dt><dd>NRTH Inc.</dd></div><div><dt>Portfolio</dt><dd>Nine ventures</dd></div><div><dt>Perspective</dt><dd>Six fields</dd></div><div><dt>Find us</dt><dd>nrth.group</dd></div></dl>
 <section class='editorial-split'><div data-enter><span class='section-label'>A way of thinking</span><h2>Stay curious.<br/>Get specific.</h2></div><div data-enter><p>A broad perspective is useful when it leads to a better question. We look at the people, information and practical constraints behind an idea before deciding what shape it should take.</p><p>Each NRTH venture has its own subject. The connection is an interest in work that could be understood differently, coordinated more thoughtfully or made easier to do.</p><a class='inline-link' href='/approach'>How we approach an idea</a></div></section>
 <section class='editorial-split section-dark'><div data-enter><span class='section-label'>Room for difference</span><h2>The point is<br/>the perspective.</h2></div><div class='disclosure-list' data-enter><details open><summary>Keep the venture focused.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>A health workflow and a transport assignment need different expertise. We give each direction its own questions and boundaries.</p></details><details><summary>Let knowledge travel.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>A useful approach to information, coordination or experimentation may inform more than one field. The opportunity is to connect knowledge without making every project the same.</p></details><details><summary>Make room to change.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>Research and conversation can sharpen an idea, reveal a constraint or suggest a different direction. The next step should follow what is learned.</p></details></div></section>
 <section class='editorial-split'><div data-enter><span class='section-label'>The worlds we work in</span><h2>Wide interests.<br/>Specific questions.</h2></div><div class='related-links' data-enter>{fields.map(field=><a href={'/projects?field='+field.name}><strong>{field.name}</strong><span>{field.ventures.join(', ')}</span></a>)}</div></section>
 <ContactInvitation headline='See something differently?'/>
</Layout>
